{"slug":"Fallout","title":"Fallout","cats":[],"headings":[{"id":"See_also","text":"See also","level":2}],"html":"<figure class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File/Thumb\"><img src=\"/images/Fallout_irradiated.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"156\" height=\"134\" class=\"mw-file-element\" data-file-width=\"156\" data-file-height=\"134\"><figcaption>Bright green <span class=\"wiki-deadlink\">fallout</span> from a <a href=\"/Hydrogen_Bomb\" title=\"Hydrogen Bomb\">hydrogen bomb</a>.</figcaption></figure>\n<p>Fallout occurs after any missile lands on ground. It irradiates the ground and leaves <span class=\"wiki-deadlink\">fallout</span>. \n</p><p>It is known for its bright green color.\n</p><p><br>\nThe <span class=\"wiki-deadlink\">fallout</span> defense modifier ranges from 2.5× to 5× based on the ratio of <span class=\"wiki-deadlink\">fallout</span> tiles on the map. <sup id=\"cite_ref-1\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-1\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>1<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup>  It can significantly increase army losses.\n</p><p><br>\nAs the&nbsp;% win condition does not take into account irradiated soil as claimed territory it may trigger a win or loss.\n</p>\n<div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading2\"><h2 id=\"See_also\">See also</h2></div>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/Missile_Silo\" title=\"Missile Silo\">Missile Silo</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/Atom_Bomb\" title=\"Atom Bomb\">Atom Bomb</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/Hydrogen_Bomb\" title=\"Hydrogen Bomb\">Hydrogen Bomb</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/SAM_Launcher\" title=\"SAM Launcher\">SAM Launcher</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/MIRV\" title=\"MIRV\">MIRV</a></li></ul>\n<div class=\"mw-references-wrap\"><ol class=\"references\">\n<li id=\"cite_note-1\"><span class=\"mw-cite-backlink\"><a href=\"#cite_ref-1\" aria-label=\"Jump up\" title=\"Jump up\">↑</a></span> <span class=\"reference-text\"><a href=\"/Combat\" title=\"Combat\">Combat#Fallout Modifier</a></span>\n</li>\n</ol></div>","section":"Combat & mechanics"}
